.TH BIOSEQ.FASTA 4 2000-1月 "MSA.of" "MSA.of"
.SH NAME
MSA.of \- Do multiple sequence alignment
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIMSA.of(\fBseqs\fR as any, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Do multiple sequence alignment
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBseqs\fB \fR\- 
 A fasta sequence collection, which can be a @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.FASTA.FastaFile\fR object, 
 a collection of the @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.FASTA.FastaSeq\fR object, or a character vector of 
 the raw sequence data.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
an @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.SequenceAlignment.MSA.MSAOutput\fR object that contains the multiple sequence 
 alignment result: the aligned sequence data of each input sequence and the 
 alignment cost value.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
bioseq.fasta
.SH FILES
.PP
seqtoolkit.dll
.PP
